Killing the gnome quickly, or following him until he's dead, will provide
you with a wand of digging that opens a path to the temple.

A randomly generated dwarf with a pick-axe may occasionally dig though
the wall of the temple; you can influence the dwarf's direction somewhat
by blocking his way.

Waiting for a giant with a boulder, or waiting for a dwarf or umber hulk
that had some boulder left behind as result of his digging activities
will provide you with a boulder to fill the hole at the temple entrance.

Trying to pass the square with the hole will occasionally succeed; keep
on trying.

Finding some means to levitate or jump (boots, rings, spells, potions) will
make it possible to pass the hole.

So much for the general purpose suggetions, and now for something specific;
knights have intrinsic jumping ability (a knights move!), so you should be
able to enter anyway!

